  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 151 PM EDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nFor this forecast period did further trend lower with pops and\nfurther pushed back timing as uncertainty remains high in the \nexact evolution of this abnormal synoptic setup. The slow \nmoving, weakening, and washed out cool frontal boundary with \nfairly low amounts of forcing and instability less than 2000 \nJ/kg is not being handled well at all by guidance. There still \nis the chance for some locally heavy rainfall at times if \nthunderstorms can develop and drift slowly along the boundary in\npretty unidirectional flow and as the environment is rich in \nmoisture with PWATs 1.5 to 2 inches available. However, the \nhigher rainfall amounts will be very localized and hit or miss \nwith the showers nature. WPC still has portions of our are under\na marginal risk for exceeding flash flood guidance tonight \nthrough Friday morning. This event sure has the earmarks of \nhaving bust potential especially with the increased uncertainty \nand a majority of the troughs energy being pushed well north of \nthe area into Canada.\n\nA pretty stagnant pattern seems to set up over the area with\ntroughing remaining in place to the north of the region and\ncyclonic to zonal flow aloft will remain over the area. This\nwill keep the high temperature trend stable with seasonal \nvalues in the low to mid 80s well into next week. There will\nalso be periods of showers and thunderstorms mainly in the\nafternoon early evening time frame but with the convective\nnature will be again a hit or miss coverage.",
